 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The gate threshold is 1.3 V min, 1.7 V typ and 2.3 V max at 25 µA. On-resistance is guaranteed at both 10 V (27 mΩ max at 5.2 A) and 4.5 V (40 mΩ max at 4.2 A). The gate takes 2.6 nC typ to reach 4.5 V with 15 V and 5.2 A on the drain, 1.1 nC of it Miller charge; in Fig 6 the plateau sits near 2.7 V. Internal gate resistance is 2.3 Ω typ. Threshold falls as the junction heats (Fig 15)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate charge waveform",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "With a constant gate current, VGS climbs to the plateau while QGS is delivered, stays level through QGD, then rises on to the final value VG; QG is the whole (Fig 14a)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "td(on) runs from VGS reaching 10 % to VDS falling to 90 %, tr from VDS at 90 % to 10 %; td(off) runs from VGS falling to 90 % to VDS rising to 10 %, tf from VDS at 10 % to 90 % (Fig 10b). With VDD = 15 V, 1.0 A, RG = 6.8 Ω and 4.5 V drive they are 5.2, 4.4, 7.4 and 4.4 ns typ."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat and current",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Mounted on one square inch of copper, junction to ambient is 100 °C/W max (99 °C/W for times under 10 s), giving 1.3 W at 25 °C and 0.8 W at 70 °C with a 0.01 W/°C derating. Continuous drain current falls from 5.2 A at 25 °C to zero at 150 °C (Fig 9). On-resistance rises about 1.6 times from 25 °C to 150 °C (Fig 4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The integral diode carries 1.6 A continuous and 21 A pulsed, drops at most 1.0 V at 1.6 A, and recovers from 1.6 A at 100 A/µs in 11 ns typ (17 ns max) with 4.0 nC typ (6.0 nC max)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and marking",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "The Micro3 outline matches JEDEC TO-236AB. The top face carries the marking X Y W LC: X the part code (I for this part), Y the year, W the work week and LC the lot code; a bar over the week marks lead-free parts, and a bar under the marking marks copper wire and halogen-free build. For weeks 1 to 26 Y is the last digit of the year; for weeks 27 to 52 Y is a letter, A for 2001 or 2011 through K for 2010 or 2020. W runs A to Z over the 26 weeks of each half year. This scheme covers parts built after 02/26/2001."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Qualification",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "RoHS compliant, with no lead, bromide or halogen; moisture sensitivity level 1."
  }
 ],
